Subject: [M150] Fix bugs in MultiBuffer::OnDataProviderEvent when Prune
 empties UrlData

Original change's description:
> Fix bugs in MultiBuffer::OnDataProviderEvent when Prune empties UrlData
>
> In MultiBuffer::OnDataProviderEvent(), move Prune() after writer_index_
> is updated and SuggestProviderState() is evaluated. Previously, Prune()
> could empty data_ and call UrlData::OnEmpty(), dropping UrlIndex's last
> reference to UrlData and destroying MultiBuffer before
> writer_index_.find(pos) was executed.
>
> Fixed: 566347711
>
> Change-Id: I9389d473e0bc3c4523d6132ece32a74633c8cb76
> Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8489395
> Commit-Queue: Eugene Zemtsov <eugene@chromium.org>
> Auto-Submit: Dale Curtis <dalecurtis@chromium.org>
> Reviewed-by: Eugene Zemtsov <eugene@chromium.org>
> Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1708523}

